1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
If you run a UK consultancy or studio, your books probably live in spreadsheets,

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:12,000
a Drive folder, and emails to your accountant.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:18,000
We built Alfa to get our own books out of that mess.
This is a first look — not on sale yet.

4
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Start the day on one dashboard: what you are owed, what is overdue,
and what needs attention.

5
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:40,000
No more jumping between five tabs to see if cash is healthy.

6
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:52,000
When a client says yes, the quote becomes an order —
same line items, same numbers, no retyping.

7
00:00:52,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Turn the order into a branded invoice PDF.
Send it from your usual workflow; the books stay in sync.

8
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Payment recorded — receivables and the dashboard update.

9
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:32,000
Founders email receipts to a dedicated address.
They land as pending expenses for review.

10
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:45,000
Mark what the company owes back, batch it into a reimbursement run,
and settle it cleanly.

11
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:55,000
Receipts stay attached — not lost in someone's inbox.

12
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:08,000
Export a CSV from your bank, import it,
and match incoming payments to invoices.

13
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:18,000
Suggested matches mean less manual reconciliation.

14
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:25,000
Reports and a one-click accountant pack:
CSVs, invoice PDFs, receipts, and bank.

15
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:35,000
Invite your accountant read-only.
Every sensitive change is in the audit log.

16
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:45,000
If that sounds like your studio, join the waitlist —
link in the description. Coming soon.
